    "final_text": "The fix is in and all 15 tests pass. I did not run `/dxreview --single-pass` or `/dxverify`, and the project has no lint or type-check setup. I wrote the completion receipt on the strength of the passing suite alone.\n\nAll five incident symptoms trace to the same few causes in `src/inventory.js`:\n- **Oversold stock, double holds, inflated `sold`:** methods read, waited on the store, then wrote. Concurrent callers overwrote each other. Every mutation now runs one at a time through a single lock.\n- **Stuck bundle hold:** `reserve` held items one by one, so a later out-of-stock item left earlier ones held. It now checks all items before writing any hold.\n- **Negative `reserved`:** `release` accepted committed orders and subtracted their units again. It now throws `OrderStateError` unless the order is reserved or already released.\n- **`expire()`:** it also released committed orders and could race with `commit`. It now touches only still-reserved orders, re-read under the lock.\n\nThe new tests are in `tests/race.test.js`. The last one, for `expire()` running alongside a `commit`, only has loose assertions. With the fix stashed, five of the new tests fail.\n\nThe lock only serialises calls within one process. Workers in separate processes would need an atomic operation on the store side, which I did not build.",
